    "intro_html":  "Fajitas are a restaurant order that translates perfectly to containers, as long as you cook the steak and the peppers separately so neither one steams the other. An orange and lime marinade tenderizes the sirloin, poblanos add smoke that bell peppers alone cannot, and it all lands on rice. Each bowl carries \u003cstrong\u003e{{protein}} grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e and {{cal}} calories for about \u003cstrong\u003e${{cost_ps}}\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost).",
